{
  "id": "extensive_game.perfect_recall",
  "title": "Perfect Recall",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "extensive_game/extensive_game_perfect_recall.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Perfect Recall</h1>\n<p>An extensive game has perfect recall for player $i$ if, whenever two nodes $x$ and\n$y$ lie in the same information set of player $i$, the earlier information sets of\nplayer $i$ encountered on histories leading to $x$ and $y$ match, and the player's\nown earlier actions also match as actions in the corresponding equivalence classes.</p>\n<p>Informally, player $i$ never forgets what they knew or which actions they\npreviously chose.</p>",
